{
  "id": "COMPOUND:41991 - PROTEIN:3966",
  "verbalization": "The compound [(5R,6R,8R,9S,10R,13R,14S,15S,17R)-17-[(1S)-1-[(2R)-4,5-dimethyl-6-oxo-2,3-dihydropyran-2-yl]ethyl]-5,6,14-trihydroxy-10,13-dimethyl-1-oxo-4,6,7,8,9,11,12,15,16,17-decahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-15-yl] acetate] appears to interact with Receptor-type tyrosine-protein phosphatase beta through a series of molecular pathways. It is a target of Phytolaccoside B, which in turn targets Serine/threonine-protein kinases Nek9, Ulk2, and Nek9. These kinases are involved in signaling pathways that regulate cellular processes such as autophagy and cell survival. The evidence suggests that the compound may act through a mechanism involving the activation or modulation of these kinases, which in turn influence the activity of the receptor-type tyrosine-protein phosphatase beta. The consistent involvement of Phytolaccoside B as a mediator across different targets implies a potential role in the compound's biological activity, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
